# Copy to `.env` for local development.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ means this is inlined into the JavaScript bundle at BUILD time,
# not read at runtime. Two consequences worth knowing before deploying:
#
#   1. It must be present when `next build` runs. On Railway it's a normal
#      service variable, which is available during the build — but a value
#      changed after a build has no effect until the service is rebuilt, not
#      merely restarted.
#
#   2. It ships to the browser. Only ever put public values behind this prefix;
#      nothing here is a secret.

# Origin of the Hono API, no trailing slash.
# On Railway, reference the server service rather than hardcoding its URL:
#   NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=https://${{server.RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN}}
NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:4000
